[ITEM]
id: BL-001
title: Normalize RT tags read from camera desc (protocol-less)
type: bugfix
status: accepted
priority: P2
created: 2026-05-31
theme: rendering

[DESCRIPTION]
scn_camera_desc.cpp deserialize wraps JSON strings for color_targets/depth_target/
tp_accum_target/tp_reveal_target in single-arg res::tag(std::string). Per res_tag.h the
single-arg ctor parses the protocol via find_first_of("://"); a string WITHOUT a protocol
yields wrong protocol/path/name slices (a malformed tag that the resolver cannot match).
So a hand-authored or legacy .desc with a protocol-less RT tag is silently broken.

[MOTIVATION]
Render targets read from desc must resolve reliably. Today protocol-less RT tags fail to
resolve (masked by the per-camera RT "legacy fallback"), which is fragile and confusing.

[ACCEPTANCE]
- RT tag fields read from camera desc resolve correctly whether or not the JSON string
  includes a "protocol://" prefix.
- Canonical RT protocol decided (likely memory:// for runtime render targets) and applied
  consistently — normalize at the desc read site if no protocol is present.
- Editor-camera RT tags at the source (e.g. __editor_depth_rt) audited for the same issue
  and normalized where they originate, so serialize/deserialize round-trips cleanly.
- No regression for RT tags that already carry a protocol.

[OUT_OF_SCOPE]
- General res::tag ctor redesign (only the camera-desc read path + editor RT sources).
- Non-RT tag fields.

